<title>UK: Mauritius sugar exports fall in January-April.</title>
<headline>Mauritius sugar exports fall in January-April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mauritius exported 106,888 tonnes of sugar in the first four months of this year, down on the 147,946 exported in the same period a year ago, the Mauritius Sugar Syndicate said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bulk of the exports went as usual to the United Kingdom, which took 95,688 tonnes compared with 135,800 in the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>Exports for April 1997 alone totalled 6,163 tonnes comparedwith 7,175 tonnes a year ago, the Syndicate said in a statement.</p>
<p>Mauritius also imported 14,110 tonnes of sugar during the January-April period, of which 4,203 tonnes came from South Africa in April. It imported a cumulative 10,983 tonnes in 1996, of which 1,092 tonnes were in April.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
